<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="Four-Eb-Theme" spTempo="205">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year: 1954
Composer: Miles Davis (credited; disputed—Eddie &quot;Cleanhead&quot; Vinson claimed authorship)
Lyricist: None — instrumental
Form: 32-bar ABAC
Key: Eb major

First recorded by Miles Davis and released on his
album Miles Davis Quartet, &quot;Four&quot; is a 32-bar ABAC
form standard that became a fixture in the hard bop
and soul jazz repertoire. The tune&apos;s composition is
officially credited to Davis, though controversy
surrounds its actual authorship, with saxophonist Eddie
&quot;Cleanhead&quot; Vinson claiming he wrote the piece.
Its straightforward yet effective structure and
swinging groove made it a favorite vehicle for
improvisation among bebop and post-bop musicians.</spComments>
